  "reading": "The empty-run control subtracts a writer only when it fires in both legs, probability ~p^2 at this rate; it pays a false red when it fires in exactly one, probability ~2p(1-p). At p=0.218 that is a residual false red of ~8.7% per run and effectively no subtraction. The control is insurance against the day the fleet writes into the worktree, not a mechanism that is doing work today.",
